# Residual symmetry in Lemma 16.5.6

The currently proved deductions specialize the common-residual construction to
L and its actual conjugate, retain the two action quotients and their central
kernels, and establish invariance under the normalizer of the component
intersection. Perfect local residuals also supply exceptional two-perfectness.

The two-centrality assembly proves the four-clause equivalence in 16.5.6(4)
from the common residual, the actual earlier local tables and coverings,
the source exclusions and the faithful opposite action. It constructs the
needed involutions in both actors. The exceptional local calculations,
normalization by the selected 16.4.2(4) conjugator and discharge of the earlier
source inputs remain separate obligations; this module does not yet assert
the full unconditional Lemma 16.5.6(1)–(4).

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.1197.
-/
